1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,150
The Value of Travel.

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:05,625
Travel makes one’s own cultural assumptions visible.

3
00:00:05,625 --> 00:00:13,337
People who have lived abroad score higher on creativity and cognitive flexibility, according to research by Adam Galinsky.

4
00:00:13,337 --> 00:00:18,350
Travel builds empathy by replacing stereotypes with real human encounters.

5
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:24,237
Visiting a different neighborhood or trying unfamiliar food exercises the same mental muscles.

6
00:00:24,237 --> 00:00:29,425
The key is curiosity and openness to experiences outside one’s comfort zone.

7
00:00:29,425 --> 00:00:34,925
The benefits of travel depend less on distance than on the traveler’s openness to difference.

